    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the driveway so responders can locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the opening, particularly at night or in low visibility conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the access drive so emergency vehicles can travel the full length without obstruction.\n• Clear overhanging branches along the access drive to maintain vertical clearance for fire apparatus and taller emergency vehicles.\n• Designate and mark a turnaround area near the main residence so arriving vehicles can reposition without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the turnaround area free of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials at all times.\n• Thin dense vegetation alongside the access drive to reduce the risk of fire spreading to vehicles moving along the driveway.\n• Maintain a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings on foot without obstruction.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area organized so it does not block the access drive or the space in front of either structure.\n• If a gate is present at the driveway entrance, install a Knox Box or provide a combination to the local fire department so responders are not delayed at entry.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road entrance and near the main residence so"
  },
