    "recommendations": "• Thin the tree cluster nearest to the structure to increase open space between the trees and the building.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the structure's exterior walls.\n• Cut back ground vegetation growing up against the base of the structure.\n• Clear brush from the area immediately surrounding the structure to widen the gap between the building and surrounding plant growth.\n• Trim overhanging branches from scattered trees near the structure so branches do not hang over the roof or walls.\n• Mow or cut low ground vegetation along the length of the driveway to keep it from crowding the travel surface.\n• Keep the driveway clear of overhanging branches along its full length so vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Thin shrubs growing along the driveway edges where they narrow the usable travel width.\n• Cut back or remove dense brush in the brush area closest to the structure.\n• Thin scattered shrubs near any outbuildings or parked equipment on the property.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from ground vegetation near the structure before dry season.\n• Keep the open green space mowed short to reduce the amount of dry grass that can carry fire toward the structure."
